<li class="log-entry">
  <%= time_at(entry.logged_at, class: "entry-time muted") %>
  <div class="entry-main">
    <%# THREE CONTROLS PER ENTRY BECAME ONE MENU (UI-cohesion slice 5). Each entry carried a red
        Delete up here and an "Add existing photo" link plus an upload button below — three action
        treatments per row, and on a project with six entries EIGHTEEN controls in one panel. The
        build log is a place to READ what you did; the things you do to an entry are occasional.
        `details.menu` is the pattern the Files page already uses for exactly this problem, and it
        is on the addon class contract, so it is the component rather than a fourth treatment.
        Discoverability is the trade and it is the one the Files page already made. %>
    <div class="entry-head">
      <details class="menu" data-controller="menu">
        <summary class="btn icon small" aria-label="Entry actions" title="Entry actions">⋯</summary>
        <div class="menu-list">
          <%= link_to "Add existing photo", new_project_attachment_path(@project, entry_id: entry.id),
                      class: "menu-item" %>
          <%# The uploader keeps its own markup: it is a button beside the hidden file input it
              opens (projects/_upload_control), so it cannot become a `.menu-item` anchor without
              losing the input it exists to carry. %>
          <div class="menu-item menu-item--host">
            <%= render "upload_control", upload_url: build_log_entry_uploads_path(entry),
                       attach_url: entry_photos_path(entry), redirect_url: project_path(@project) %>
          </div>
          <%# THE CONFIRM NAMES THE ENTRY (2026-11-02, the UX audit's §H: every confirm is "Verb
              named-object?"). An entry has no title, so its first words stand in for one. %>
          <% gist = entry.body.to_plain_text.squish.truncate(48) %>
          <%= button_to "Delete entry", build_log_entry_path(entry), method: :delete,
                        class: "menu-item danger",
                        form: { data: { turbo_confirm: gist.present? ? "Delete the entry “#{gist}”?" : "Delete this empty entry?" } } %>
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
    <%# A div, not a p: Action Text emits block-level markup and a <p> cannot legally contain it. %>
    <div class="entry-body"><%= entry.body %></div>

    <%# A PHOTO OPENS ITS FILE (2026-11-02, the UX audit's C8): it was a `span`, a picture of a file
        with no way to it. Now the same link a Photos cell is — the file page, a click to open and a
        double-click for a new tab (FilesHelper#file_open_data) — named by the file, because an
        image whose own alt is empty would leave the link without a name. %>
    <% photos = entry.file_attachments.select { |a| @page_nodes.key?(a.node_id) } %>
    <% if photos.any? %>
      <div class="entry-photos" data-controller="thumbs" data-thumbs-url-value="<%= thumbnails_files_path %>">
        <% photos.each do |att| %>
          <% name = @page_nodes[att.node_id].name %>
          <%= link_to file_path(att.node_id), class: "entry-photo file-cell", title: name, "aria-label": name,
                      data: file_open_data(thumb_cell_data(att.node_id, "IMG")) do %>
            <%= render "files/thumb", thumb: @page_thumbs.thumb(att.node_id), ext_label: "IMG",
                       url: preview_src(@page_thumbs.thumb(att.node_id)) %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    <% end %>

  </div>
</li>
